\documentclass{report}
\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}
\title{Pluvial Flood Hotspots in a Coastal City:\\A Drainage Capacity Audit}
\author{M.~Okafor and H.~Lindqvist}
\date{June 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\tableofcontents
\input{chapters/background}
\input{chapters/model}
\input{chapters/results}
\end{document}

\chapter{Results}
Sixteen inlets fall below capacity for the ten-year storm.
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
\hline
District & Inlets below capacity \\
\hline
Old harbour & 5 \\
Railway quarter & 4 & urgent \\
Garden suburb & 3 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
The old harbour district alone accounts for nearly a third
of the modelled basement flooding volume.

